{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"operations\":[{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-return-trigger-link\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-return-trigger-link\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-16\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Assessing whether return or destruction is required when the agreement or protected evaluation ends.\",\"inspection\":\"Identify both the required act and its trigger. Termination or expiration qualifies, as does an expressly stated conclusion, rejection, or abandonment of the evaluation or business possibility. A request-only duty or a party's mere decision not to proceed does not qualify without language making an end event itself the trigger.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the operative return-or-destruction duty and the language establishing its end-event trigger. Include every independent termination-triggered return or deletion obligation relied upon.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[331,238,245,262,588,538,177],\"rationale\":\"Clarifies the separating trigger that was missed for express conclusion or rejection in 331 and 177, while excluding request-only duties in 538 and the mere decision-not-to-proceed formulation in 588.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-negotiation-existence-secrecy\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-negotiation-existence-secrecy\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-10\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement restricts disclosure of negotiations, discussions, a contemplated transaction, the agreement itself, or the existence of dealings.\",\"inspection\":\"A prohibition on revealing that negotiations or discussions exist establishes the hypothesis. A prohibition on public announcements concerning the agreement or transaction also qualifies; definition text alone must be paired with an operative nondisclosure duty.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the operative prohibition and the protected fact, retaining any governing introduction needed to connect a listed fact to the prohibition.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,88,588,538,136],\"rationale\":\"Adds the independently sufficient public-announcement formulation missed in 136 while preserving the need for an operative restriction rather than definition text alone.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-universal-identification-condition\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-universal-identification-condition\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-1\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Confidential-information coverage is conditioned on marking, designation, or identification by the disclosing party.\",\"inspection\":\"Confirm that the identification condition grammatically governs every covered disclosure mode. A single terminal condition may govern an enumeration of oral, written, and electronic modes; different procedures may also govern different modes. Do not treat nature- or circumstances-based coverage as identification.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the complete definition or all clauses needed to show that every disclosure mode is subject to identification by the disclosing party.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,88,331,238,136],\"rationale\":\"Makes explicit that one trailing identification condition can govern all enumerated modes, separating the entailment in 331 from genuine contextual alternatives in 88, 238, and 136.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-copy-permission-explicit\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-copy-permission-explicit\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-17\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Assessing whether the receiving party may make a copy in some circumstance.\",\"inspection\":\"Require an affirmative operational copying route, such as copies necessary for authorized use or acknowledged automatic backups. A prohibition phrased as applying without prior consent or approval is not by itself an affirmative permission to copy.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite language affirmatively authorizing, requiring, or acknowledging copy creation and its governing condition; disclosure or access permission is insufficient.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,245,177,136],\"rationale\":\"Separates affirmative copying routes in 334, 245, and 136 from consent-qualified prohibitions labeled Contradiction in 490 and 177.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-unqualified-copy-ban\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-unqualified-copy-ban\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-17\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement prohibits copying confidential information and contains no affirmative operational copying route.\",\"inspection\":\"A direct copy ban, including a ban stated as applying without prior consent or approval, negates the benchmark permission hypothesis when the complete agreement does not otherwise authorize necessary copies, backups, or another copying circumstance. Do not convert the consent qualifier itself into affirmative permission.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Contradiction\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the copy prohibition and verify across the agreement that no affirmative operational-copy or backup route qualifies it.\",\"source_operations\":[]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,245,177,136],\"rationale\":\"Corrects the polarity distinction exposed by 490 and 177 while allowing affirmative operational exceptions in 334, 245, and 136 to be handled by the complementary permission skill.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-explicit-nontechnical-coverage\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-2\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The confidential-information definition enumerates subject matter or data categories.\",\"inspection\":\"Find an expressly covered non-technical category, such as business, financial, marketing, personnel, customer, contact, or transaction information. Generic references to all information, documents, analyses, form, or derivatives do not alone prove non-technical coverage.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Contradiction\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the definition and at least one explicit non-technical category; include continuation text when the category list crosses fragments.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,88,331,245,262,588,538,177,136,187],\"rationale\":\"Captures the repeated explicit-category contradictions while excluding the overbroad inferences from derivative documents in 588 and writing-related language in 187.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-independent-development-permission\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-12\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement contains an exclusion, reservation, or acknowledgment concerning independent development.\",\"inspection\":\"Confirm that the receiving party may develop information independently without using or accessing the protected information. Prior approval to disclose, lawful receipt, or another unrelated exception does not establish independent development.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the independent-development clause with its governing exclusion or reservation language when needed to make its legal function complete.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,88,331,238,245,588,538,177,136,187],\"rationale\":\"Provides a positive substantive test for the many entailments and excludes the unrelated prior-approval clause incorrectly used in 177.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-third-party-acquisition-permission\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-13\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement addresses information obtained from an external source or made available non-confidentially.\",\"inspection\":\"Look for lawful receipt from a source other than the disclosing party that is not bound by confidentiality, or for the disclosing party's later non-confidential release making the information externally available. Independent development and consent to the receiver's own disclosure are different matters.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the external-source or non-confidential-release clause and its governing exclusion introduction, including any condition concerning the source's authority or confidentiality duties.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,88,238,245,588,538,177,136,187],\"rationale\":\"Distinguishes genuine external acquisition clauses missed in 588 and 136 from independent development or receiver-disclosure approval mistakenly relied on in 177.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-oral-information-inclusion\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-3\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The definition or coverage clause addresses communication form.\",\"inspection\":\"Determine whether oral or verbal communication is expressly within confidential information, including language covering information irrespective of communication form or information disclosed in writing and also orally. Do not infer oral coverage merely from derivative notes or documents.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the language linking oral, verbal, or form-independent communication to confidential-information coverage, with any necessary definition continuation.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,331,238,245,588,538,177,136,187],\"rationale\":\"Directs attention to the actual modality language, avoiding the derivative-document substitution seen in 588 while covering the varied oral formulations in the successful witnesses.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-employee-nonsolicitation\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-18\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement restricts recruiting, hiring, employment contact, or solicitation involving personnel of the disclosing party.\",\"inspection\":\"Find a prohibition on soliciting, employing, hiring, or initiating employment contact with officers, employees, or other personnel. Proxy solicitation, transaction standstill language, and general contact restrictions are not personnel nonsolicitation unless tied to employment or hiring.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the operative employment-related prohibition and the covered personnel class; include duration, targeting limits, or recruiting exceptions when they qualify the prohibition.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,588,538],\"rationale\":\"Adds the absent inspection for explicit employee nonsolicitation clauses missed in 588 and 538, while separating them from irrelevant proxy-solicitation candidates visible in 334 and 538.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-survival-end-event-link\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-19\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement states that duties continue beyond an end event or remain effective for a post-event period.\",\"inspection\":\"Verify that confidentiality, non-use, or another agreement obligation continues after termination, expiration, completion, abandonment, or an equivalent end of the protected relationship. Continuation merely after return or destruction does not establish survival of agreement termination.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite both the continuing obligation and the termination, expiration, completion, abandonment, or equivalent end event to which continuation is linked.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,331,238,245,262,588,538,177,136,187],\"rationale\":\"Separates genuine post-end survival across the positive witnesses from the return-or-destruction continuation clause that produced the false positive in 588.\"}],\"noop_reason\":null}"}}
